h him; and [the king] sent a man before him: before the messenger came to him, he also said to the elders, Do ye see that this son of a murderer has sent to take away my head? See, as soon as the messenger shall have come, shut the door, and forcibly detain him at the door: [is] not the sound of his master's feet behind him?"],["33",[["ἔτι",705538,28],["αὐτοῦ",702165,102],["λαλοῦντος",708071,152],["μετ᾿",708780,0],["αὐτῶν",702165,40],["καὶ",707031,7],["ἰδοὺ",706497,88],["ἄγγελος",700140,4],["κατέβη",707202,2],["πρὸς",710844,0],["αὐτὸν",702165,85],["καὶ",707031,7],["εἶπεν",705373,2],["ἰδοὺ",706497,88],["αὕτη",709858,107],["ἡ",709436,10],["κακία",707054,12],["παρὰ",709995,0],["κυρίου",707996,18],["τί",712867,126],["ὑπομείνω",713219,207],["τῷ",709436,113],["κυρίῳ",707996,114],["ἔτι",705538,28]],"While he was yet speaking with them, behold, a messenger came to him: and he said, Behold, this evil [is] of the Lord; why should I wait for the Lord any longer?"]]